    "narrative": "Our offense is positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.06) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.63). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most potent asset; beyond his elite baseline, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Valdez and a slow delivery, which significantly boosts his stolen base probability in a category where we remain hyper-focused on efficiency. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** earns a \"Strong\" designation by exploiting a favorable matchup against Houser; his +18% SP skill adjustment and +10% platoon advantage make him a mandatory start, especially with his aggressive profile on the basepaths. **Dylan Beavers** (64.33) and **Bryce Harper** (63.56) round out our top-tier core, both offering high-floor profiles against right-handed pitching that should provide stability to our daily scoring.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **JJ Bleday** (49.20), who narrowly missed the cut. While **JJ Bleday** offers a solid baseline, he is hampered by a significant -14% adjustment against Castillo. We ultimately prioritized the higher situational upside of **Lawrence Butler** (56.21) and **Justin Crawford** (51.51); despite **Justin Crawford** hitting 9th, his ability to manufacture runs via speed keeps him ahead of **JJ Bleday** in our scramble for stolen bases. We are keeping a close watch on **Lawrence Butler**, who faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Rasmussen (3.17 xERA). If the wind patterns shift or the lineup structure changes, we have the flexibility to swap him for **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.01), though the platoon disadvantages currently keep both on the fringes of our optimal lineup. We are avoiding exposure to elite arms elsewhere to preserve game caps, specifically shielding the bench from Rasmussen's strikeout-heavy profile.",
